{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.65,
            0.049,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Proportional Reasoning–2"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.088,
            0.67,
            0.11
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ How do we mark the different slices of the pie chart?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": "To mark a slice in the pie chart, the angle corresponding to a grade should be proportional to the number of students who have scored that grade. The total angle in a circle is 360°. So, we need to divide 360 in the ratio of $1 2 : 1 0 : 8 : \\bar { 6 } : 4 .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.189,
            0.595,
            0.212
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Can we reduce this ratio to its simplest form?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.214,
            0.847,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "We can use the same procedure we used to reduce a ratio with two terms to its simplest form. We divide all the terms by their HCF to get the simplest form."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.27,
            0.846,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "In this example, 2 is the HCF of the terms. We get the simplest form by dividing all the terms by 2. The ratio becomes 6 : 5 : 4 : 3 : 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.307,
            0.358,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "So, the angles are:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.339,
            0.79,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Grade}A=\\frac{6}{(6+5+4+3+2)}\\times360^{\\circ}=\\frac{6}{20}\\times360^{\\circ}=6\\times18=108^{\\circ}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.376,
            0.673,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": "Grade $\\mathrm{B}=\\frac{5}{(6+5+4+3+2)} \\times 360^{\\circ}=5 \\times 18=90^{\\circ}.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.409,
            0.454,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "Grade C = 4 × 18 = 72°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.44,
            0.456,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": "Grade D = 3 × 18 = 54°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.471,
            0.452,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": "Grade $\\mathbb{E} = 2 \\times 18 = 36^{\\circ}.$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.503,
            0.649,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "Now let us construct a pie chart using these angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.537,
            0.485,
            0.575
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Step 1: Draw a circle and mark the radius AB as shown below:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.576,
            0.378,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.489,
            0.537,
            0.816,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": "Step 2: To draw the slice to represent the proportion of students who got an A grade, measure 108° from the segment AB on A (anti-clockwise), and mark the new radius AC."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
